+++ b/e2e/faults/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Own real fault controls
+
+These controls are infrastructure only. They never replace processors, guards, AdminClient or Toolkit storage.
+Component smoke evidence does not certify CP/KVS/Playmaker or managed transport.
+
+## Kafka
+
+`OwnedAuthorizationBroker.start()` starts a separate random-project KRaft broker from
+`compose.authorization.yaml`; `bootstrap()` is its real plaintext endpoint. No principal is a
+super user. The disposable broker uses StandardAuthorizer and default allow only before ACLs exist.
+`denyTopic(exactRunPhysicalTopic)` grants Cluster All (including Alter for ACL restoration), then
+installs Cluster Create DENY and exact Topic All DENY for User:ANONYMOUS. The cluster denial prevents
+the cluster-level CreateTopics permission from bypassing a topic denial. It affects only this
+independent cluster. `restoreAuthorization()` removes the installed denials. `close()` removes the
+cluster volumes/network and certifies zero Docker resources under its exact project label.
+
+`OwnedKafkaFaults.open()` verifies project/service/owned/run labels from the launcher's explicit
+DOCKER_CONTEXT, E2E_COMPOSE_PROJECT, E2E_COMPOSE_FILE and E2E_ENV_FILE. `reduceToThreeBrokers()` stops
+only broker4/broker5, retaining three KRaft controllers; `restoreBrokers()` observes five live nodes.
+`close()` restores after test failure. This is a run-wide control; scenarios run sequentially.
+Kafka CREATE can still assign RF5 to registered, fenced brokers while only three nodes are alive;
+the component check records reduced ISR and its later restoration. For CP insufficient-live-broker
+coverage, use UPDATE/RF reconcile: the real KafkaTopicReplicationFactorAdjuster checks live
+`describeCluster().nodes()` before reassignment. A separate one-node auth cluster has no additional
+registered brokers and rejects native CREATE RF2.
+
+Kafka reference: [3.9 official authorization and API permission documentation](https://kafka.apache.org/39/security/authorization-and-acls/).
+
+## Fury Toolkit KVS
+
+`ToolkitSandboxFaults.open(generatedPrefix)` takes the exact generated `KEY_VALUE_STORE_*` prefix
+(v1/v2 as injected), requires a physical `sbox...` mapping and dedicated BC/instance metadata.
+It starts read/write HTTP proxies and creates a new empty owned SCP artifact directory.
+Pass `childEnvironment()` only to `RealControlplaneProcess.start(overrides, properties)`; the child
+continues to use the normal Toolkit builder and physical sandbox container. No globals are mutated.
+
+Toolkit 1.0.5 wire contract inspected from the resolved jar:
+
+- GET read URL + `/containers/<physical>/<URLEncoder-encoded key>`.
+- SAVE POST write URL + `/containers/<physical>`; JSON contains key/value and TTL header.
+- CAS PUT write URL + `/containers/<physical>/<encoded key>`; original `x-kvs-versions` and
+  `x-kvs-ttls` headers are forwarded. Value is a string from bytes, not Base64.
+
+`RealHttpFaultProxy.Rule(method,pathContains,bodyContains,phase,action,hits,holdSeconds)` matches only
+selected real requests. The physical sandbox container must be an exact decoded path token.
+`REQUEST` observes arrival before forwarding; `RESPONSE` observes the actual upstream response
+before delivering it to Toolkit. `HOLD` pauses until `release()` or aborts on its bounded deadline.
+`abortHeld()` cancels held requests without forwarding and is also used by close.
+`RESET` aborts the connection; `FAIL503` injects a transport/server failure and never a fake success.
+`hits` permits bounded repeated failures across Toolkit retries. The convenience HOLD constructor
+holds up to 1000 matching retry attempts; RESET/FAIL503 default to one. Rearming a later window
+cannot revive an aborted prior request. Select terminal CAS using method
+PUT + exact guard key path + bodyContains `COMPLETED`/`FAILED` (state value, after JSON escaping).
+`awaitReached(deadline)` observes a counter, so crash windows do not depend on sleep timing.
+
+For a real post-send/pre-finalize action crash, hold the terminal CAS at REQUEST, independently
+observe the result broker record and actual PUBLISH_PENDING KVS record, kill the CP child,
+`abortHeld()` (never release the pre-forward terminal CAS), and restart/redeliver. For save/CAS accepted but response lost, hold at RESPONSE and independently
+read actual KVS before crashing the child. Neither control claims transactional delivery.
+
+## Transport
+
+`RealHttpFaultProxy.startTcp(ownedLoopbackPort)` forwards real bytes to an explicitly owned loopback
+server. TCP REQUEST/RESPONSE HOLD/RESET windows or `resetConnections()` affect only its own sockets.
+Use it only where all protocol destinations stay proxied: Kafka advertises broker addresses, so a
+bootstrap-only TCP proxy does not intercept subsequent direct broker connections. Kafka producer
+failure uses scoped own broker ACLs or own broker reduction; never claims bootstrap-only coverage.
+
+All listeners bind 127.0.0.1. Upstream URLs come from trusted generated exports and are fixed per
+process. Headers, bodies, keys, tokens and URLs are never recorded in proxy evidence/logs. Closing
+reaps only its own child and certifies both listener ports closed. Missing config fails; no fallback.
