+# Functional SPEC — real Playmaker cleanup and KVS observation (T25/T26)
+
+Independent source review found that current Playmaker E2E cleanup deletes action/DP-lock keys before quiescence and executes SQL cleanup even if the CP fixture gate fails. Live PM listeners may save an action after a test deleted it; actual resurrection has not been executed. DLT injection also lacks durable process/resource intent. Repair these source defects before expanding or certifying physical Playmaker scenarios.
+
+A run-owned PM process must be identified and recorded durably before it can serve fixture work. Record the initial process and every restart with exact PID/start identity/source/JAR/run/port/parent provenance. A recycled or unverifiable PID is never deletion authority. Parent cleanup must recover restart leases after Gradle failure. Do not kill by app name, port or shared process tree.
+
+Before the first SQL seed, PM HTTP dispatch or neutral DLT send, persist the owned resources/correlations/transport offsets intended by that fixture. Stop/reap the exact own PM process before destructive SQL/KVS cleanup. Keep CP/Kafka alive while proving actual bridge commits, CP worker completion and stable tails; both actual PM result-topic/group offsets must match the final tails. Pending, unobservable or changed tails fail and retain; never seek/commit artificially to manufacture caught-up state. Process shutdown is not a deployment-success certificate.
+
+One common gate precedes every CP/PM key, SQL, topic/group or private-config deletion. UNKNOWN is sticky: preserve resources/journals and independently close safe clients, but block destructive database.close, Sandbox retirement and next-fixture restart. Cleanup verifies every registered own row/key/resource; failures are aggregated without discarding journals. Each next fixture starts a freshly identified own PM process only after complete prior cleanup.
+
+Observe productive KVS calls passively for negative cases without emitted UUIDs. Delegates must remain current Toolkit clients against exclusive Sandbox exports. Record nonsecret mutation attempts durably before delegation and observe completion/failure for sync/async/batch/CAS/delete operations. A stale zero snapshot, memory-only counter or unwrapped consumer cannot prove no write. Verify the effective beans consumed by CP guard and PM repositories; retain on unknown observer state. Never store business results in the observer, change exports/endpoints, swallow Toolkit exceptions or replace its backend.
+
+Acceptance: peer review reproduces safety negative controls and identity/journal/trap behavior from a clean checkout, observes real own process lifecycle where possible, compiles all physical suites and ultimately executes/repeats full real CP/PM families. Component controls do not certify PM/KVS business. Existing external gates and SOURCE_ONLY limitations remain visible. No shared resource mutation, new dependency, authentication semantic change or production effect is authorized by this fixture repair.
+
+
+## V4 independent worker and canonical source gates (2026-10-02)
+
+Register the actual native JUnit worker before constructors/fixtures in every mandatory local family, even when productive applications are separate processes and the worker opens no productive KVS context. Completion requires nonempty/no-failure/no-skip tests and the pinned Gradle owner's actual normal wait. Missing worker/owner binding fails; zero productive KVS contexts is permitted only for that independent worker proof. Every actual productive generation still requires its separate close and process-exit proofs.
+
+Canonical PM permits only exact reviewed profile-selection annotation deltas in seven existing productive files. Routes, auth and bodies stay byte-identical to the identified baseline. Final parent proof failure durably publishes UNKNOWN before reconciliation inspection; storage failure still retains and fails.
+
+
+## V4.1 independent final gate (2026-10-02)
+
+Every independently invoked all-final gate requires the typed current task completion and native workers, including families whose productive applications are external. Missing or corrupt summary/task/owner/worker proof cannot authorize cleanup. Preserve the existing native child-generation behavior while correcting its compile defect.
+
+
+## V4.1r2 — typed native identity and neutral control readiness
+
+Approved bounded delta: a native worker owner PID is a positive JSON integer, never bool/float/string. Neutral controls wait for actual durable guardian registration and STOPPED lease in addition to process absence; all outcomes/assertions/deadlines remain unchanged. Source/neutral checks still do not certify productive business or backend.
