+# T25 proposed owned Playmaker lifecycle
+
+PLANNING_ONLY. No implementation, Gradle, API, Docker/provider activity or physical certification. Parent must record the SPEC and approve exact author paths before writing. The independent source findings remain in `t25-playmaker-cleanup-source-v1/review.md`; T23 guard/oracle review is complete separately.
+
+The selected fence is to stop and reap the exact run-owned PM process for each fixture, then restart the same immutable bootJar for the next fixture. This avoids claiming ownership of global PM threads. Stopping PM alone does not prove that its result backlog is drained or that a remote request settled; those have separate fail-closed gates.
+
+## Proposed exclusive paths
+
+All paths are relative to the CP worktree. No PM production source, build.gradle or existing protocol/auth helpers need changes.
+
+1. NEW `e2e/PlaymakerProcessOwner.java`: JDK25 standard-library guardian/CLI, outside Gradle. Owns actual `Process` instances, exact birth identity, a private Unix socket and durable launch lease; performs bounded stop/reap and restart.
+2. MODIFY `e2e/playmaker-runner.sh`: build and pin the PM jar/source, register the guardian before any PM fork, export its private control-directory reference, and stop/reap the current persisted generation in the parent trap. The existing `run.sh` trap already calls this function before its retention/destruction decisions; no change to `run.sh` is planned.
+3. NEW `src/e2eTest/java/com/mercadolibre/rio_controlplane_kafka/reale2e/playmaker/OwnedPlaymakerLifecycle.java`: typed guardian client, durable per-fixture inventory and intents, real Kafka offset/group observation, and immutable cleanup permit.
+4. MODIFY `src/e2eTest/java/com/mercadolibre/rio_controlplane_kafka/reale2e/playmaker/PlaymakerKafkaE2ETest.java`: acquire one PM generation, journal before SQL/HTTP operations, bind actual response IDs, and replace unconditional deletes with the ordered gate/cleanup below.
+5. MODIFY `src/e2eTest/java/com/mercadolibre/rio_controlplane_kafka/reale2e/playmaker/OwnedPlaymakerDatabase.java`: journal every planned SQL identity before seed/update, explicit permit-required destructive cleanup, independent non-destructive `close()`, and absence assertions for every owned table, including deployment_log.
+6. MODIFY `src/e2eTest/java/com/mercadolibre/rio_controlplane_kafka/reale2e/playmaker/PlaymakerResultTransportE2ETest.java`: the same lifecycle and pre-send DLT intent, exact source/DLT/probe IDs and actual send offset, PM halt, and post-halt CP/bridge/offset gates. Neutral invalid input stays a transport test, not a fabricated business result.
+7. MODIFY `src/realIntegrationTest/java/com/mercadolibre/rio_controlplane_kafka/reale2e/support/RealE2eFixture.java`: one narrowly fail-closed API, proposed `retainUnverifiedPlaymakerWork()`, sets `quiescenceVerified=false` and durable sticky `UNKNOWN/PLAYMAKER_LIFECYCLE_UNVERIFIED`. It grants no cleanup override. Invoke before fixture.close whenever the PM fence/gate is uncertain. A PM-only journal otherwise protects the parent but does not stop the current CP fixture's deletes.
+8. NEW `e2e/tests/playmaker-lifecycle-contract.py`: L0 ownership/filesystem/process contract fixtures using real neutral private child processes; no PM/KVS/domain mocks. Wire into the existing root harness only by a separately approved root edit after these paths freeze.
+
+## Ownership and startup
+
+The shell creates a private 0700 control directory and reconciliation directory, validates no symlinks/foreign UID, and starts the JDK guardian independently of Gradle. The guardian lease is durable before PM can start or any owned MySQL provisioning can begin. Prepare jar/source information before PM fork, or retain a BOOTSTRAP lease with incomplete preparation rather than claiming a started process.
+
+Copy the prepared actual bootJar into the owned runtime directory, preserve 0600 permissions and hash it. Record its canonical path/SHA256 and the exact PM source commit plus source-manifest hash; git HEAD alone must not hide dirty source. Every restart revalidates the immutable jar/source tuple.
+
+Write launch phase STARTING before `ProcessBuilder.start()`, force the file, atomic move and force the directory. Then persist run, guardian PID/startInstant, PM actual PID/startInstant, generation UUID, jar/source identity, port, group and private config paths before declaring READY. Missing PID/start identity, a changed path/hash or STARTING interrupted between fork and durable PID is UNKNOWN; it cannot be declared absent or safely cleaned.
+
+The guardian uses inherited private child environment plus explicit scoped overrides and fixed properties; it never prints environment, token, SQL/body or KVS values. Socket requests contain only bounded typed control data; no arbitrary shell command, jar replacement or environment payload is accepted. Only one fixture owns a generation. Fixed source/runtime identity and private lease references are signal authority for this process only, never authority to delete arbitrary paths or namespaces.
+
+Use the actual effective group `e2e_<run>_playmaker_results`, explicitly supplied as `spring.kafka.consumer.group-id`. The existing real-e2e YAML overrides the runner's `PLAYMAKER_KAFKA_GROUP_ID=e2e_<run>_playmaker`; that export cannot be used as proof of the effective result group. Own source and action/deployment listener annotations both resolve the Spring property. Validate real broker group membership/assigned partitions before dispatch; never identify it by a group-name prefix alone.
+
+The guardian observes the exact Gradle worker PID/start identity registered by BEGIN and the exact parent launcher PID/start identity. Their loss triggers an independent PM stop/reap and sticky UNKNOWN. Parent trap first uses the live guardian, then a validated exact persisted PID/start tuple if the guardian is unreachable; it does not trust a stale shell pm_pid after restarts. If identity cannot be validated, retain and fail rather than signal a possibly reused PID. All cleanup stages execute independently even if one throws/interruption occurs.
+
+## Fixture intent and transitions
+
+Proposed typed API: `beginFixture(fixtureId, exactWorkerIdentity)`, `beforeSqlMutation(ids)`, `beforeHttpDispatch(path, ownedIds)`, `bindObservedResponseIds(ids)`, `beforeDltSend(source,dlt,probeId)`, `stopAndReap(deadline)`, `verifyStoppedOffsetsAndAbsenceInputs(...)`, `cleanupPermit()`, and `finishVerifiedCleanup()`.
+
+Persist OPEN before any business SQL seed/update, authenticated HTTP dispatch or DLT producer.send. The ledger records fixed run/fixture/generation IDs; exact SQL row IDs/table relationships; known deployment/action IDs and corresponding CP/PM keys; exact bootstrap/topics/group/ports; owned container/project and Sandbox/routing references. It contains no business payloads, credentials or values. Every intent/response-ID binding forces file and directory. HTTP with an uncertain response/correlation ID remains UNKNOWN; never adopt, scan or delete global null-shaped keys to compensate.
+
+The PM lease and fixture journal have separate fixed filenames (`pm-lease-<UUID>.json`, `pm-fixture-<UUID>.json`). Existing parent `reconciliation-status.py` treats any retained JSON as unsafe. These names do not weaken the CP fixture's existing exact `retained-*.json` parent/child handshake. The narrowly restrictive CP API above transfers PM uncertainty into its own existing UNKNOWN guard.
+
+UNKNOWN is sticky and forbids new dispatch, cleanup permits, deletes and restarts. An assertion failure with fully known stopped work may still clean safely, but cannot publish PASS. A timeout, forced stop with unsettled work, missing intent/PID, unknown provider outcome, failed barrier or unknown observation persists UNKNOWN before any destructive cleanup.
+
+## Ordered cleanup and restart barrier
+
+1. Disable further fixture dispatch and close/flush its own producers; all test HTTP calls must finish. A real pre-stop PM group-offset read can reduce avoidable backlog but is readiness only, never the cleanup certificate.
+2. Guardian stops the exact PM generation (TERM, bounded wait, then force/reap if necessary), verifies the recorded process/subtree identities are absent and the exact own listening port is closed. Forced termination or an unsettled external call does not silently become safe; retain UNKNOWN where its outcome cannot be proven.
+3. Only after PM is dead, invoke the existing actual CP/bridge barrier: all trigger partitions committed to current tails, exact CP observer identity and actual executor idle, then trigger-tail recheck. No terminal KVS/SQL state or transient idle snapshot substitutes for this barrier.
+4. With a separate real Admin client, require the exact PM result group to have no active members and inspect every partition of both deployment and action result topics. Require actual committed offset >= current latest offset, then recheck all tails/partition sets and CP/bridge state. No seek, artificial commit, reset, group deletion or skipped record is allowed. An absent commit is not fabricated as 0: proposed bounded exception is `NULL_AND_PHYSICALLY_EMPTY` only when actual earliest=latest=0 for that partition; every other absent commit or pending tail is UNKNOWN. Parent SPEC must explicitly accept that empty-partition exception or choose strict rejection.
+5. Require the run-owned MySQL server to show zero PM-user sessions after process reap, so outstanding PM statements are not inferred complete from JVM death alone. Unknown observations or unexpected fixture-related table rows retain. No KVS delete is allowed if a tracked write/request is unsettled.
+6. Only after all gates pass, close/verify CP fixture cleanup first. If it fails, retain the PM journal and skip PM KVS/SQL deletion. Issue an immutable permit bound to run, fixture, generation, process birth identity and exact observed inventories. PM action/lock deletes and explicit SQL cleanup require that permit and verify actual absence per known key and every owned table. A partial deletion failure retains FAILED/UNKNOWN evidence and cannot restart.
+7. Independent client close still runs on every path. Remove journals only after complete verified absence, force the directory, and keep original failure evidence. Restart the pinned PM jar only when the previous fixture has no retained work, process/port absence is verified and both result-topic tails are still covered. A new late tail invalidates restart; it is not consumed or acknowledged merely to make cleanup pass.
+
+Parent shutdown independently stops every persisted own PM generation even when Gradle dies, then relies on the existing any-JSON retention gate before MySQL/Kafka/runtime/config/Sandbox destruction. Remove the guardian lease only after guardian/process absence and all fixture journals have been verified retired; an open/unknown launch cannot vanish merely because the child is no longer alive.
+
+## Verification boundary
+
+Before author freeze: syntax/diff checks, private JDK compile, real private filesystem force/permissions, exact PID/start/run rejection, STARTING/abandoned Gradle-worker journal retention, real neutral own-process stop/reap/parent-trap and interrupted-cleanup tests. These are L0/component tests only. Separately reproduce Kafka offset gating against real owned Kafka with genuine producer/consumer commits and pending tails; never mocked Admin success.
+
+Domain independently reviews the implementation and ownership/UNKNOWN call sites after freeze. Full PM/CP/KVS physical execution remains NOT_EXECUTED until its existing credentials/Sandbox gates permit it; no component or source result is promoted to a business certificate.
