+# Functional SPEC — real Playmaker Kafka frontiers (T24)
+
+The complete CP E2E assignment includes the ten PM-KAFKA capability IDs added after focal canonical-master discovery. Their executable fixture preparation must continue despite the Fury Sandbox clone403. This feature complements 20261001-real-e2e and never promotes a prepared or compiled body to a physical capacity PASS.
+
+Observe real authenticated PM HTTP operations, actual owned MySQL relations/definitions/slots/history, SDK1.5 Kafka trigger wire, CP1.3 production processing, actual Kafka effects, productive Toolkit claims/results and PM terminal state. Configuration/inheritance operations alone must leave physical Kafka and CP dispatch/claims/results unchanged. Explicit deployment must correlate every stage and preserve the separation between desired entity assignments and infrastructure provisioned by CP.
+
+Prepare connect/reconnect, same-source revision update/no-op, removal/disconnect with provenance preservation, explicit/omitted/new/missing environment footprints, real concurrent relation writes/rollback, entity validation, inherited-config deployment/failure, source-specific template exclusions, optional/oversize pipeline context and version-specific authorization. Use the existing 351-row matrix IDs; do not invent provider membership or resolve product support through test expectations. Literal kafka inheritance and direct CP ACK-ignore are separate boundary tests: they are not a successful PM-to-CP deployment journey. A local GCP transport overlay does not certify canonical Materializer routing or GCP OAuth.
+
