+# Current canonical Playmaker Kafka frontier — source revalidation
+
+Canonical PM master is now **0c83575c54cb198d238be7d83f3b4d8de27abbc8**, release202610.1.0 merge#1247; old master was3cd0daf6e17841ab79381f1eb5e2bd014ad68bd1. Develop remains7673f4bffc286f0f24d4214938df53c4c5eb9c38; work checkpoint1b4b8e1554c37357e4b39e1860be6ad43f9aa640 remains based on that develop. No checkout, rebase, implementation, matrix or repository-doc edit was made. This audit adds source evidence only; all real PM→CP→Kafka/KVS journey outcomes remain NOT_EXECUTED.
+
+Primary evidence is git show/diff on those exact objects. Selected blob identities and equalities are in pm-current-master-frontier-blobs.json. File/line refs below are relative to src/main/java/com/mercadolibre/rio/playmaker/ at canonical0c83575 unless a different SHA is explicit.
+
+## What changed in canonical master, versus what was already in the tested base
+
+The old→current master release adds Kafka entity inheritance, optional entity assignment provenance and environment-filtered catalog/import metadata. The inheritance service/resolver/EntityAssignment/EntityRelationInput, both deployment producers, optional deployment context builder/dispatch adapter, Service peek client/services and deployment/action result domain handlers are **byte-identical between current master and develop767**. Their release to master does not mean they were exercised by our20 PM rows: those rows cover component deploy/redeploy/delete, actions, Service peek and neutral local-result DLT, not topology/entity inheritance or pipeline-context dispatch.
+
+Both production BigQueue deployment producers now exclude local-integration: restclient/impl/BigQueueDeploymentTriggerProducerImpl.java:21 and service/pipeline/impl/DeploymentTriggerProducerImpl.java:19. Actual profile local & local-integration uses canonical localintegration/LocalKafkaDeploymentTriggerProducer.java:17–20, which implements both producer interfaces and publishes raw SDK DTO JSON keyed deployment_id with actual broker ACK at45–59. These classes and LocalKafkaDeploymentResultListener are already identical in develop767. Local canonical deployment transport therefore needs no new implementation or rebase. Managed BigQueue ACK/retry/OAuth/consumer/result-to-PM persistence remain a separate unexecuted frontier; local Kafka equality cannot certify them. The newly prepared work Action local transport remains a candidate addition, not canonical master.
+
+## Kafka/entity contract now canonical
+
+EntityInheritanceServiceImpl.java:82–114 follows only active relations from the changed catalog-signal; PipelineConfigPatchServiceImpl.java:147–179 and288–304 invokes it inside the config-version/slot transaction, after actual entity validation at151–153. Relation connect/disconnect invokes it at PipelineRelationsServiceImpl.java:180–192. A repeated active connect still asks for a delta; no delta writes no new definition.
+
+EntitySlotResolverImpl.java:36–80 projects the signal's first OUT into an IN slot specific to that source and an OUT only if no OUT already exists, or updates an OUT inherited from that same source. Slots carry assignment.slotId UUID, state INHERITED and sourceComponentId (154–167); same-source updates preserve slotId (65–76). Missing signal OUT or disconnect removes only that source's INHERITED slots (38–41,83–99); OVERRIDDEN/DECLARED and other sources remain. EntityAssignment.java:18–20 and EntityRelationInput.java:18–22 make assignment optional; the resolver currently creates INHERITED only, not owner-override/declared provenance.
+
+EntityInheritanceServiceImpl.java:125 and268 acquires the Kafka row lock before reading/merging its active definition; currentParams at343–349 reads that active definition rather than a missing/stale environment slot. It preserves other physical Kafka params in the same map before creating a new config version at296–303. Explicit environment advances that one slot; omitted environment uses distinct existing ServiceModel footprint (240–247), and no footprint persists only the definition (196–207). Config-save propagation can create an undeployed slot via advanceSlot318–339. ServiceServiceImpl.java:341–392 only updates/creates the SQL slot, status not started; **this is not physical Kafka creation or a CP deployment**. The next real deploy must carry the preserved Kafka params plus entities through the actual trigger/result chain.
+
+Imported-component first-slot creation is rejected at ServiceServiceImpl.java:370–378. Invalid explicit environment is resolved before relation writes at PipelineRelationsServiceImpl.java:157–163; pipeline-version mismatch fails upfront121–124. EntityRelationValidationServiceImpl.java:44–70 rejects malformed/duplicate input locally, then positive relations require real EntityServiceClient getEntity/getSchemaVersions at73–99 and a real existing revision. Real MySQL plus Kafka/KVS alone cannot replace that service for positive entity-validation certification. No mock/entity-service fixture is authorized by this evidence.
+
+**Template frontier:** Constants.java:124–135 maps only aws-msk-topic and literal kafka into the inheritance Kafka family; gcp-kafka-topic and kafka-topic are absent. CP canonical430 application.yml:123/134 accepts aws-msk-topic,gcp-kafka-topic,kafka-topic, not literal kafka; DeploymentTriggerController.java:97–100 ACK-ignores an unconfigured type. Thus GCP inheritance and the generic kafka↔kafka-topic name boundary need an explicit product/routing contract. Generic Kafka-family membership in PM is not proof the current CP can deploy that raw template. Existing GCP CRUD rows do not cover this distinction.
+
+## Context, DTO, result and Service peek boundary
+
+Pipeline DispatchRequestFactory.java:64–82 builds PROVISION with optional ComponentContext; context derivation failure is caught and drops only optional context at91–115. BigQueueDispatchAdapter.java:39/114–170 measures the complete candidate, retains context through200KiB, discards it above that or on measurement failure, and publishes the same params/schema/id afterward. ComponentContextService.java:101–165 snapshots owner/component/latest version and related source/destination outputs, including imported-slot resolution. Legacy component deployment uses the no-context constructor at DeploymentServiceImpl.java:1014–1031. Our20 PM tests exercise that legacy path; they do not certify pipeline context, relation/import snapshots or its size guard.
+
+SDK canonicalad2 DeploymentTriggerMessage.java:25–39/62–86 explicitly keeps params as operation configuration and context as an optional snapshot; CURRENT remains1 (DeploymentSchemaVersion.java:31). CP resolved SDK1.3.1 SHAa16585a1f16a04a8b48e9cf010b6f16919a15deab3c46df9c2ee9ed10b5a600e has no typed ComponentContext and ignores unknown properties. Consequently new context can be wire-shape compatible and silently unavailable to CP; CP's privacy observation of unknown context is not preservation/semantic adoption. entities survives as opaque params data on the DTO, but CP KafkaParams/GcpTopicParams consumes physical topic/partitions/RF/retention, not an entity-schema provisioning feature. Do not claim CP manages entity schemas or changes topic schema state.
+
+Service peek and result-domain classes have no old-master→current-master or develop→current-master delta. ServiceActionsServiceImpl.java:63–69/141–203 obtains the actual latest deployment output topic_name (typed wrapper/suffixed keys supported); KafkaControlPlaneClientImpl.java:63–87 still sends configured msk-brokers-url, not provider-specific output.servers/OAuth routing. Current MSK Service-peek preparation stays applicable to the exact common source. It does not become a managed GCP Service-peek certificate.
+
+## Authorization version frontier
+
+The new release did not change the following versus old master3cd, but **current master and tested develop767 differ materially**. Current ActionServiceImpl.java:132–134 uses additive requireIfConfigured; ActionAuthorizationService.java:72–81 calls the external operation authorizer only when a permission exists. ConfiguredActionPermissionProvider.java:18–33 uses exact pair then wildcard; no permission means no additional ACME call. Develop instead has declared-read/dispatch-family rules and fail-closed unknown Actions. Current pre-creation Action dispatch at ActionServiceImpl.java:195–232 verifies DP existence and publishes null component/environment/context without the develop pre-creation read-action allowlist. Tiger-authenticated controller remains at ActionController.java:76–95/122–134. CP unsupported action and unmapped null environment outcomes must be observed downstream, never assumed to be a valid PEEK.
+
+Current ComponentDeploymentServiceImpl.java:302–304 skips extra permission authorization if team/project is blank; develop did not. Develop also has an extra persisted deployment-slot/DP ownership check absent from current master. Pipeline config/relation mutation keeps its legacy PipelineAuthorizationService/assertWriteAccess and Tiger checks, but not develop's new configured operation guard/owner lock revalidation. A successful authenticated work/develop journey therefore cannot certify canonical master's permission-denied, owner-change or pre-creation frontier. This report does not propose a security-semantic change.
+
+## Missing Kafka-join rows to add explicitly, not to promote existing families
+
+All proposed rows start coverage NONE/test_prepared=no/status NOT_EXECUTED; none has an executable full chain or verified real-service fixture yet.
+
