+| Deployment component_id, data_product_id, environment_id | @NotNull; OpenAPI/Swagger required | Normal producers supply resolved IDs and reject absent component/DP/environment. Missing-input COMPLETED is a validation gap; prepare a regression requiring rejection before business effects. |
+| Deployment component_name, data_product_name, environment_name | @NotNull; manual OpenAPI/Swagger omit these properties entirely | Producers pass resolved model names, with no intentional null. Model name columns themselves are nullable in the Java mapping, an upstream risk rather than an explicit optional event contract. SDK-required/documentation-omission gap; do not call COMPLETED valid. MSK missing environment_name already returns downstream INVALID_PARAMS, not proof of inbound validation. |
+| Deployment criticality, published_at | @NotNull; OpenAPI/Swagger required | PM defaults resolved criticality to LOW (or explicit MEDIUM for inactivation) and creates a real timestamp. No intentional null found. COMPLETED for omitted/null metadata contradicts the declared requirements. |
+| Deployment deployment_group_id | @NotNull; OpenAPI/Swagger required | Explicit conflict: legacy PROVISION/DEPROVISION/inactivation intentionally send null, whereas pipeline dispatch carries a UUID. Preserve legacy compatibility until resolved; keep separate from invalid metadata. |
+| Action data_product_id, triggered_at | @NotNull; generated Swagger required | Normal and pre-creation producers supply actual DP identity and Instant.now. No intentional null found. Missing-input COMPLETED is a validation gap. |
+| Action triggered_by | @NotBlank; generated Swagger required/minLength1 | Producer uses validated Authentication.getName. Null/omitted and blank need a failure regression; no intentional-null path found. |
+| Action component_id, environment_id | @NotNull; generated Swagger required | Explicit conflict: normal existing-component actions supply IDs, but documented pre-creation intentionally sends null for both. Arbitrary malformed PEEK success is not a blanket contract. Split normal/pre-creation cases and resolve supported routing/policy before adding a guard. |
