+# T25 independent Playmaker cleanup source review
+
+CHANGES_REQUESTED_SOURCE_ONLY: two P2 findings. No Gradle, source edits, API/Docker/provider execution or physical certificate. Eleven bounded source snapshots and hashes are retained; unrelated concurrent T23 metadata edits can shift fixture lines.
+
+1. PlaymakerKafkaE2ETest88–100 deletes actions:<id> and dp-action-lock:<DP> before fixture.close. Its107–114 loop always attempts database.close even after fixture cleanup/quiescence failure; OwnedPlaymakerDatabase150–157 deletes deployment/history/service/definition/component/environment/DP rows without consulting UNKNOWN. Thus a retained CP journal cannot prevent destructive PM cleanup.
+2. Test setup68 registers only CP port/trigger bridge. RealE2eFixture336–400 waits own CP HTTP/process/threads and bridge trigger commits (694), without PM listener/executor/scheduler/ingress or PM result group offsets. Own PM Java remains running throughout Gradle204; launcher stops it only in exit trap run117/runner134. PlaymakerResultTransportE2ETest62 publishes before any PM journal intent, then78 closes only neutral probe clients and84 reports launcher-owned transport, without PM quiescence certification.
+
+Concrete source interleaving: PM LocalKafkaActionResultListener38 invokes the real consumer; ActionResultConsumerServiceImpl39 reads an existing action. Before its45 save, teardown deletes the same key and89 observes absence. The consumer can then save through ActionKvsRepositoryImpl76, recreating the key after absence was certified. No synthetic business result is needed. Late SQL handling is also outside the gate, but guaranteed SQL resurrection or a physical reproduction is not claimed.
+
+Safe executable architecture must first persist own PM intent before SQL seed/dispatch/DLT send and record exact resources/IDs where known; unresolved effects remain UNKNOWN. Then either fence owned PM ingress and every producer source, drain actual owned domain executors/schedulers/listeners and current result offsets with tail rechecks plus CP/bridge quiescence, or stop/reap the exact owned PM process before deletion and restart it for the next fixture. The latter is the narrower initial option and avoids inventing global thread ownership. Terminal KVS/SQL or a transient idle snapshot is insufficient. Only a verified fence/reap plus independent absence permits SQL/KVS deletion or journal retirement. Gate failures retain PM inventory, SQL, KVS, namespaces and configuration; safe independent client close still runs.
+
+Implementation is not authorized; SPEC/path contract and T23 review take precedence. This proves unsafe call ordering and an uncovered worker boundary from source only. The initial reviewer check failed because class Javadoc mentioned Playmaker; the corrected check inspects the actual quiescence method and its diagnostic remains preserved.
